1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,748
Restrictions Lifted 

2
00:00:03,360 --> 00:00:05,702
What... What has he done?

3
00:00:05,702 --> 00:00:08,771
To inject himself with the Beast Virus...

4
00:00:08,771 --> 00:00:10,405
He must be out of his mind.

5
00:00:18,241 --> 00:00:21,211
S... So this is... the power of the beasts!

6
00:00:21,211 --> 00:00:22,743
U-Uncle Hefty!

7
00:00:22,743 --> 00:00:24,035
What about your vaccine?!

8
00:00:24,035 --> 00:00:26,903
I'm... better off without it!

9
00:00:26,903 --> 00:00:28,458
Jun! Let me out now!

10
00:00:28,458 --> 00:00:29,437
But you're still...!

11
00:00:29,437 --> 00:00:30,254
Please.

12
00:00:31,505 --> 00:00:35,144
Your body is in great danger, Heavy Iron! You need to receive proper treatment immediately!

13
00:00:35,144 --> 00:00:38,260
I'm not the weak Heavy Iron you knew... 

14
00:00:38,260 --> 00:00:39,594
ANYMORE!

15
00:00:39,877 --> 00:00:43,704
This is real bad! That old man finally went crazy! What do we do, Jun?!

16
00:00:43,904 --> 00:00:45,177
Come back, Heavy Iron!

17
00:00:49,413 --> 00:00:50,178
You...!

18
00:00:50,178 --> 00:00:51,158
Blue Cop! Come back inside!

19
00:00:51,158 --> 00:00:51,707
Jun!

20
00:00:52,007 --> 00:00:54,854
Tigun, Set Up! Tiger Cannonade!!

21
00:00:57,568 --> 00:00:59,347
I'll go... fight too...!

22
00:00:59,347 --> 00:01:02,401
You already used up all of your energy! You can't even stand up straight!

23
00:01:02,401 --> 00:01:05,386
But... I can't just let that guy get away with this...!

24
00:01:05,386 --> 00:01:06,703
We can use this!

25
00:01:06,703 --> 00:01:07,272
What's that...?

26
00:01:07,272 --> 00:01:11,140
An emergency recovery injection kit! Mega Ambler gave it to me just in case something unexpected happens.

27
00:01:11,140 --> 00:01:12,897
That Scrooge of a bot just gave you that for free?

28
00:01:12,897 --> 00:01:16,028
No. I had to trade him ten alternators from some used cars.

29
00:01:16,370 --> 00:01:19,528
Thank you. Soleil, I'll fight until the end!

30
00:01:19,528 --> 00:01:21,934
Alright. Please use that on him, Mr. Edd!

31
00:01:21,934 --> 00:01:22,968
Leave it to me!

32
00:01:22,968 --> 00:01:27,114
Whaddaya say we buy them some time? I'm really good at annoying Uncle Heavy!

33
00:01:27,114 --> 00:01:29,518
Bzzt! If that's all it takes, I got your back!

34
00:01:29,518 --> 00:01:31,996
I'm counting on you, guys! Tigun! Time for a substitution!

35
00:01:31,996 --> 00:01:33,376
Phantom Hornet! Set Up!

36
00:01:34,029 --> 00:01:35,473
Shadow X! Set Up!

37
00:01:35,873 --> 00:01:37,825
Yo, Tiger! Pass me the baton!

38
00:01:37,825 --> 00:01:38,994
You did great out there!

39
00:01:38,994 --> 00:01:40,284
Don't let me down, you two!

40
00:01:41,528 --> 00:01:43,057
Get yourself together, old-timer!

41
00:01:43,557 --> 00:01:46,932
You wanna get even stronger? You're too dang greedy, man!

42
00:01:46,932 --> 00:01:49,616
Even Captain Hook would call you out for cheating next time he sees you!

43
00:01:50,152 --> 00:01:51,639
Those prattling brats...!

44
00:01:52,704 --> 00:01:54,147
Wait, he can fly now??

45
00:01:54,147 --> 00:01:55,277
Now he's really cheating!

46
00:01:55,277 --> 00:01:58,874
Bzzt! Doesn't matter! With a body that big, he probably can't go any faster than a crawl!

47
00:02:01,573 --> 00:02:03,170
Is that... Heavy Iron?!

48
00:02:03,170 --> 00:02:05,643
What is going on over there? Let's hurry!

49
00:02:05,643 --> 00:02:07,362
Just a little bit more!

50
00:02:17,468 --> 00:02:19,562
Just a little bit... and you're done!

51
00:02:20,689 --> 00:02:22,683
Phantom Hornet! Get out of there!

52
00:02:23,674 --> 00:02:24,841
Where do you think you're going?

53
00:02:33,676 --> 00:02:34,480
Fire Roar-

54
00:02:34,480 --> 00:02:36,003
-Blaze!!

55
00:02:38,378 --> 00:02:45,005
The power of the wild is like the blood we're born with. I will never forgive anyone who abuses it!

56
00:02:45,005 --> 00:02:48,463
How dare you lecture me, you big-mouthed lion cub!

57
00:02:48,463 --> 00:02:49,755
Now, Blaion!!

58
00:02:54,920 --> 00:02:55,792
Shadow X!

59
00:02:55,792 --> 00:02:57,406
Heli-Tornado!!

60
00:02:58,903 --> 00:03:02,978
You should know better than anyone that this move won't work on me.

61
00:03:02,978 --> 00:03:05,659
Oh, I know! So how about this, then?

62
00:03:05,659 --> 00:03:07,568
Omega Heat Flame!!

63
00:03:10,982 --> 00:03:14,307
Why are you doing this, Heavy Iron?! I thought we were getting along just fine!!

64
00:03:14,307 --> 00:03:16,662
I even wonder myself... Why did I do that...?

65
00:03:16,662 --> 00:03:17,765
What are you-?!

66
00:03:17,765 --> 00:03:21,214
Let's see just how strong this new power truly is!

67
00:03:26,131 --> 00:03:28,339
Let's get out of here! Something's not right about his increase in energy!

68
00:03:29,194 --> 00:03:31,551
Jun. I think this is all we can do...

69
00:03:31,551 --> 00:03:34,830
I should have saved your friend like I saved Blue Cop, but I failed once again...

70
00:03:34,830 --> 00:03:36,408
I'm sorry.

71
00:03:36,408 --> 00:03:38,340
There's no need to apologize. Shadow X!

72
00:03:38,340 --> 00:03:39,896
Uncle...!

73
00:03:40,096 --> 00:03:41,252
Blaion, you too!

74
00:03:41,752 --> 00:03:42,906
How shameful...!

75
00:03:58,620 --> 00:03:59,970
Everyone is going to die if I don't do something!

76
00:03:59,970 --> 00:04:00,481
Soleil!!

77
00:04:00,481 --> 00:04:01,446
What are you doing?!

78
00:04:03,378 --> 00:04:05,947
Heavy... Dragon...!!

79
00:04:08,711 --> 00:04:11,974
[System limitations removed. Activating repulsion-lift.]

80
00:04:13,147 --> 00:04:14,435
...Breath.

81
00:04:34,380 --> 00:04:36,360
Wh-what just happened?

82
00:04:37,902 --> 00:04:39,115
Soleil!!

83
00:04:47,452 --> 00:04:48,568
No!!

84
00:04:48,568 --> 00:04:50,248
She won't budge an inch!

85
00:04:54,106 --> 00:04:55,169
Let's get outta here, Jun!

86
00:05:00,260 --> 00:05:03,990
What a fool. That's what happens when you fire off all of your energy in one shot.

87
00:05:03,990 --> 00:05:05,163
What was that?

88
00:05:05,163 --> 00:05:09,064
But I admire the guts it must've taken to try wielding the power of the beast on your own.

89
00:05:09,064 --> 00:05:11,265
Say, why don't we join forces?

90
00:05:11,265 --> 00:05:14,799
Heh. I prefer working alone. But...

91
00:05:14,799 --> 00:05:17,351
It just so happens I have some questions for you.

92
00:05:18,877 --> 00:05:21,739
It might not be so bad to accompany you for a little while.

93
00:05:21,739 --> 00:05:23,212
Ask me anything and everything.

94
00:05:23,212 --> 00:05:25,586
But first! Let's grab ourselves something to eat.

95
00:05:26,786 --> 00:05:29,040
Soleil uses an anti-gravity system to regulate her weight to 38.5 kilograms,

96
00:05:29,040 --> 00:05:32,894
which is the approximate average weight for someone your age.

97
00:05:32,894 --> 00:05:34,582
Anti-gravity system?

98
00:05:34,582 --> 00:05:36,709
She's actually heavier than a compact car.

99
00:05:36,709 --> 00:05:38,872
That system is the only way to make her appear like a normal child.

100
00:05:38,872 --> 00:05:46,635
She used it to protect all of you. I think her body froze because the surge protector device activated to protect her electronic brain.

101
00:05:46,635 --> 00:05:48,528
So she wasn't human...

102
00:05:48,528 --> 00:05:50,353
That's right. She's an android...

103
00:05:50,353 --> 00:05:51,714
that I created.

104
00:05:52,379 --> 00:05:56,467
Then what about that thing you said before? You said Soleil was Crest's little twin sister!

105
00:05:56,467 --> 00:05:57,531
I did.

106
00:05:57,531 --> 00:05:59,695
It was all a lie that my mother made up.

107
00:05:59,695 --> 00:06:01,809
Why did you have to lie like that?

108
00:06:02,923 --> 00:06:04,176
Because I was heartbroken!

109
00:06:04,176 --> 00:06:07,628
My own son befriended a robot from another planet and he didn't even tell me.

110
00:06:07,628 --> 00:06:11,502
If you're talking about Wild Guardy, I promised him that I'd keep him a secret from everyone.

111
00:06:11,502 --> 00:06:14,070
Even so, you could've come to your own mom for advice.

112
00:06:14,070 --> 00:06:17,780
It doesn't matter if you're my mother. Telling you would mean breaking my promise to him!

113
00:06:17,780 --> 00:06:21,651
Anyway, he made me so jealous that I decided to find another Metal Cardbot for myself.

114
00:06:21,651 --> 00:06:22,603
What???

115
00:06:23,101 --> 00:06:26,554
I painstakingly combed through every location known to have been struck by meteorites.

116
00:06:26,554 --> 00:06:28,580
And that's when I finally found him...

117
00:06:28,580 --> 00:06:31,106
Fallen into the glaciers of Antarctica, there lay Blaion!

118
00:06:31,606 --> 00:06:36,052
Thanks to the research data our son studied first, it was very easy to wake Blaion up.

119
00:06:36,052 --> 00:06:37,848
Ungh...! Augh...!! 

120
00:06:39,733 --> 00:06:40,579
Who...? 

121
00:06:41,930 --> 00:06:43,441
Thank you. Because of you, I'm still alive.

122
00:06:43,441 --> 00:06:45,811
Kyahaa!! It spoke! It spoke!!

123
00:06:45,811 --> 00:06:47,782
Ahem... That's not how this should go.

124
00:06:47,782 --> 00:06:52,347
I'm the one who should be thanking you! I'm so happy to finally meet a new Metal Cardbot!!

125
00:06:52,347 --> 00:06:55,165
I'm a Wild Cardbot. I'm nothing like their kind.

126
00:06:55,165 --> 00:06:56,370
Wild Cardbot?

127
00:06:56,370 --> 00:06:59,675
Are they really different? Come to think of it, your eyes don't look the same as a Metal Cardbot's!

128
00:06:59,675 --> 00:07:01,917
You also have sharp claws on your hands!

129
00:07:01,917 --> 00:07:05,089
What's that on your back? Is it something important?

130
00:07:05,089 --> 00:07:08,713
This is an artifact that our tribe has passed down since ancient times.

131
00:07:08,713 --> 00:07:11,403
Perhaps I will be its last heir.

132
00:07:11,937 --> 00:07:14,235
Oh? Something just fell from you. 

133
00:07:15,115 --> 00:07:17,633
Nnngh... My, how curious!

134
00:07:17,633 --> 00:07:20,499
That is a Metal Breath. Only the chosen ones can wield it.

135
00:07:20,499 --> 00:07:21,835
Chosen ones?

136
00:07:21,835 --> 00:07:25,075
It refers to those who will not deceive or exploit our people who have come from a distant star. 

137
00:07:25,075 --> 00:07:28,047
It also refers to someone with whom we can communicate heart-to-heart, and who holds purity within.

138
00:07:28,047 --> 00:07:31,353
Madam, we received a call from headquarters.

139
00:07:31,353 --> 00:07:32,759
Thank you, Soleil.

140
00:07:32,759 --> 00:07:34,824
Hi, it's me. What's up?

141
00:07:35,265 --> 00:07:37,483
Madam, you dropped this.

142
00:07:37,483 --> 00:07:38,345
Did you just-?!

143
00:07:38,345 --> 00:07:40,267
Is there something wrong, Madam?

144
00:07:40,836 --> 00:07:44,067
Soleil was originally a butler robot that I built.

145
00:07:44,067 --> 00:07:48,398
But I thought that if I did some research into how she can use the Metal Breath, I might be able to accomplish more through her.

146
00:07:48,398 --> 00:07:51,894
And that's how Soleil was reborn as my daughter.

147
00:07:51,894 --> 00:07:54,658
And I also added a little sprinkle of me and my son's DNA to her-

148
00:07:54,658 --> 00:07:56,521
Ah. Any further details are confidential.

149
00:07:56,521 --> 00:07:58,488
Um... Sorry. My brain can't keep up with all of this.

150
00:07:58,488 --> 00:08:02,113
It means she implanted fake memories in her mind to trick her into thinking she's my sister.

151
00:08:02,113 --> 00:08:03,984
Trick her? That's a little too far, son!

152
00:08:03,984 --> 00:08:05,487
Why did you have to do that?

153
00:08:05,487 --> 00:08:09,894
I always wanted to have a daughter. Crest had already moved out of the house,

154
00:08:09,894 --> 00:08:14,101
and it was my dream to go shopping or traveling with a cute daughter of my own.

155
00:08:14,101 --> 00:08:16,028
She reminds me of my mom when she met Peruru...

156
00:08:16,028 --> 00:08:16,645
Goodness...

157
00:08:16,645 --> 00:08:19,413
Blaion, did you already know about Soleil?

158
00:08:19,413 --> 00:08:24,502
Yes. We're all called "machine lifeforms" by the people of this planet, so it doesn't matter what Soleil is, right?

159
00:08:25,002 --> 00:08:26,844
Mother has always been like that.

160
00:08:26,844 --> 00:08:29,785
She's very opinionated, and doesn't listen to what others are saying.

161
00:08:29,785 --> 00:08:31,743
Things must've been tough for you.

162
00:08:31,743 --> 00:08:34,901
Soleil thinks that you're her real brother, right?

163
00:08:34,901 --> 00:08:39,238
Yes, until now. I'm a little bit worried for her, now that she has found out her true identity.

164
00:08:39,238 --> 00:08:42,146
Aww, you're worried? You're a great big bro!

165
00:08:42,966 --> 00:08:46,039
Come. You need to rest. We can set up a contingency plan tomorrow.

166
00:08:46,039 --> 00:08:46,761
Sure.

167
00:08:52,064 --> 00:08:55,645
Ahh. You know what they say, a Wild Cardbot runs on sheer meal power. 

168
00:08:56,045 --> 00:08:58,229
Alright, I got the rough idea of what's been going on around here.

169
00:08:58,229 --> 00:09:00,612
A coexistence between Metal Cardbots and little fleshlings?

170
00:09:00,612 --> 00:09:04,537
A so-called outlaw would never be satisfied with such a pathetic game of peace.  

171
00:09:04,537 --> 00:09:07,968
I just wanted to know the limits of my power.

172
00:09:07,968 --> 00:09:12,359
You’re even more of a Wild Cardbot than the ones following that little fleshling kid.

173
00:09:12,359 --> 00:09:15,802
How dare they even talk about peace when my home planet and my people are all gone?

174
00:09:15,802 --> 00:09:19,446
I'd rather follow the calling of my own instincts! Am I right, brother?

175
00:09:19,446 --> 00:09:23,734
Instincts... Yes. I feel freer than ever before.

176
00:09:23,734 --> 00:09:25,291
That's what I'm saying!

177
00:09:25,291 --> 00:09:29,969
Well, now that we filled our fuel tanks, I'd say it's time we show the people here a new world order.

178
00:09:29,969 --> 00:09:33,048
And to do that... we'll take out the head honcho first!

179
00:09:33,648 --> 00:09:35,050
Sigh...

180
00:09:35,050 --> 00:09:37,951
How do I explain this to Anna and Theo?

181
00:09:37,951 --> 00:09:41,880
Let's tell them once things settle down. It seems you need to organize your thoughts, too.

182
00:09:42,178 --> 00:09:43,013
Argh!!

183
00:09:45,255 --> 00:09:48,497
No way! There's nothing to organize! I have one thought only!

184
00:09:48,497 --> 00:09:50,639
Blue Cop! Let's go see Soleil!

185
00:09:51,339 --> 00:09:53,129
Mother, what is this...?

186
00:09:53,129 --> 00:09:54,713
It's Blue Cop's biometric information.

187
00:09:54,713 --> 00:09:58,797
Thanks to Soleil sealing him the other day, I was able to collect some precise data. 

188
00:09:58,797 --> 00:10:00,514
What are you trying to do now...

189
00:10:00,514 --> 00:10:01,491
Look here!

190
00:10:01,491 --> 00:10:05,138
Whether before or after transformation, this part sits completely unused!

191
00:10:05,138 --> 00:10:09,184
It's similar to what I discovered on Blaion's body when I first found him!! What could it possibly be?!

192
00:10:26,168 --> 00:10:28,533
W-what do you think you're doing?

193
00:10:28,533 --> 00:10:30,643
So you're the chieftain of Mowtown!

194
00:10:30,643 --> 00:10:32,452
We'll be taking your palace!

195
00:10:32,452 --> 00:10:33,492
What?!

196
00:10:33,492 --> 00:10:37,513
What if I put this part right here? No, right there?

197
00:10:37,513 --> 00:10:38,439
- [Breaking news.]
- Ahaha! This is so much fun!

198
00:10:38,439 --> 00:10:39,470
-  [The Motown City Hall has been taken over by Metal Cardbots...]

199
00:10:39,470 --> 00:10:40,402
-  [The Motown City Hall has been taken over by Metal Cardbots...]
- Mother!

200
00:10:40,402 --> 00:10:44,793
Huh? Jun and Soleil didn't show up today. What could've happened to them?

201
00:10:44,793 --> 00:10:47,093
Anna, you hear anything from Jun?

202
00:10:47,093 --> 00:10:50,671
Nothing. Uncle Edd did tell me that the plan failed though...

203
00:10:50,671 --> 00:10:51,559
WHAT?!

204
00:10:51,559 --> 00:10:55,031
Uh... Teacher! Turn on the TV! Like, right now!

205
00:10:56,150 --> 00:10:56,923
What's going on?

206
00:10:56,923 --> 00:11:01,679
[To all officers throughout Mowtown. City Hall has been seized. I repeat, City Hall has been seized!]

207
00:11:01,679 --> 00:11:02,859
Mowtown City Hall...

208
00:11:02,859 --> 00:11:04,371
...has been seized?!

209
00:11:04,371 --> 00:11:07,714
[Can you see them? Two Metal Cardbots are standing atop City Hall!]

210
00:11:07,714 --> 00:11:08,610
Solid Horn and... 

211
00:11:08,610 --> 00:11:09,586
Heavy Iron?

212
00:11:09,586 --> 00:11:11,195
[Over there! We have visuals on a person...]

213
00:11:11,195 --> 00:11:14,205
[Wait! Mayor Jacques is tied up with chains!]

214
00:11:14,205 --> 00:11:15,179
DAD!!

215
00:11:15,179 --> 00:11:17,320
We are the Wild Cardbots.

216
00:11:17,320 --> 00:11:19,691
Your chieftain is now in our hands.

217
00:11:19,691 --> 00:11:24,161
Surrender Mowtown to us peacefully! If you choose to resist, we’ll gladly take you down!

218
00:11:24,161 --> 00:11:25,697
Oh, my my. Isn't this a big problem?

219
00:11:25,697 --> 00:11:27,626
Tch... Solid Horn...!

220
00:11:27,626 --> 00:11:29,755
Oh, Soleil!

221
00:11:29,755 --> 00:11:32,212
Hey there, my sweet daughter, how are you feeling?

